# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Local config. The client ID is a public identifier rather than a secret
# (PKCE, no client secret), but it points at one specific dashboard app, so it
# stays out of the repo — .env.example is the committed template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Android wrapper build output. The wrapper scripts themselves — android/gradlew
# and android/gradle/ — are committed on purpose: they are how the build pins
# its own Gradle version on a machine that has none.
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties

# Release signing. The keystore is kept in the working tree, at
# android/klangkiste.jks, so it sits beside the build that uses it — but it must
# never reach a commit, because this repository is public and a leaked signing
# key cannot be un-leaked. A pre-commit hook backs these rules up; see the
# README, since .git/hooks is not cloned.
#
# Careful with `git clean -xdf`: -x deletes ignored files, which includes the
# keystore. Losing it is not recoverable — an APK signed with a different key
# installs as a different app rather than as an update, with new identity and
# empty storage. Keep a copy off this machine.
android/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
